past.description:
As CEO, spearheaded the transformation of Avara Pharmaceuticals, a Private Equity owned $350MM pharmaceutical CDMO (contract development and manufacturing organization) with plants in Norman, Oklahoma; Aiken, South Carolina; Arecibo, Puerto Rico; Reims, France; Shannon, Ireland; Bristol, UK; Liscate, Italy; Montreal, Canada; 

• Challenges: Negative EBITDA and extreme cash burn by legacy big pharma plants that had been acquired from Merck, Pfizer, UCB, Astellas, AstraZeneca, Novartis, Sandoz; poor supply agreements; high legacy cost structure; negligent oversight and governance.

• Results: Created $32MM Y/O/Y improvement in annualized EBITDA, returning company to profitability in 12 months. Restructured organization, renegotiated supply contracts, successfully oversaw completion of FDA and other global regulatory agency audits, restarted plant struggling with quality issues, reorganized global organizational chart, insourced IT and technology, reduced headcount, invested strategic capex into winning operations, divested poor performers, recruited global business development team. Won back customers and recruited new ones. Negotiated 50% volume increase in key supply contract. Restructured $150 million in debt.
